<div class="pd-calendar-documentation">

	<section id="overview">
		<h2 class="doc-section">Overview</h2>
		<p>
			<code>PDCalendar&lt;TItem&gt;</code> shows anything that has a start and an end in time on a calendar. It is
			generic over your own item type and reads everything through selector delegates, so there is no calendar
			model to convert into.
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li>Three views: a <strong>Month</strong> grid, a <strong>Week</strong> time grid with an hour axis, and an <strong>Agenda</strong> list for narrow screens.</li>
			<li>Overlapping items in the week view sit side by side, using greedy column packing.</li>
			<li>Items spanning midnight, or several days, appear on every day they cover.</li>
			<li>A <code>TimeZone</code> decides which day and hour an item falls in, and daylight saving days are drawn with their true 23 or 25 hours.</li>
			<li><code>OnVisibleRangeChanged</code> tells the host what to load, and <code>IsLoading</code> shows the busy overlay meanwhile.</li>
			<li>Keyboard accessible, with ARIA grid roles, and no JavaScript unless <code>ScrollToHour</code> is set.</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section id="examples">
		<h2 class="doc-section">Examples</h2>

		<DocExample Title="Basic usage"
					AnchorId="basic-usage"
					Code="@_basicCode"
					Language="razor"
					DemoStyle="min-height: 420px;">
			<DemoContent>
				<PDCalendar TItem="Meeting"
							Items="_meetings"
							StartSelector="m => m.Start"
							EndSelector="m => m.End"
							TitleSelector="m => m.Title"
							Date="_date"
							View="CalendarView.Month" />
			</DemoContent>
			<Description>
				<p>
					Supply the items and the two time selectors; everything else has a default. The date and view
					are two-way bindable with <code>@@bind-Date</code> and <code>@@bind-View</code>.
				</p>
			</Description>
		</DocExample>

		<DocExample Title="Lazy loading"
					AnchorId="lazy-loading"
					Code="@_lazyCode"
					Language="razor">
			<DemoContent>
				<p class="text-muted">The Demo tab loads a two-station radio schedule this way, with a deliberate delay so the busy overlay shows.</p>
			</DemoContent>
			<Description>
				<p>
					<code>OnVisibleRangeChanged</code> is raised when the calendar is first shown and whenever the range it
					shows changes, whether by navigation, a new view or a new date. The range runs from the start of the
					first visible day to the start of the day after the last, in the calendar's time zone, so it is ready
					to use as a half-open query. The calendar lays out only the items inside its range, so the host may
					supply just those.
				</p>
			</Description>
		</DocExample>
	</section>

	<section id="parameters">
		<h2 class="doc-section">Parameters</h2>

		<h5>Data</h5>
		<table class="table table-sm">
			<thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>Items</code></td><td><code>IEnumerable&lt;TItem&gt;?</code></td><td>The items to show.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>StartSelector</code>, <code>EndSelector</code></td><td><code>Func&lt;TItem, DateTimeOffset&gt;?</code></td><td>Required. When an item starts and ends; an end before the start is treated as the start.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>TitleSelector</code></td><td><code>Func&lt;TItem, string&gt;?</code></td><td>The title; defaults to <code>ToString()</code>.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>KeySelector</code></td><td><code>Func&lt;TItem, object&gt;?</code></td><td>Identifies an item, so the selection survives reloading items as new instances.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>CssClassSelector</code></td><td><code>Func&lt;TItem, string?&gt;?</code></td><td>Extra classes for an item, for example to set <code>--pd-calendar-item-bg</code>.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>TooltipSelector</code></td><td><code>Func&lt;TItem, string?&gt;?</code></td><td>Hover text; defaults to the title and times.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>IsDisabledSelector</code></td><td><code>Func&lt;TItem, bool&gt;?</code></td><td>A disabled item is shown but cannot be selected.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>ItemTemplate</code></td><td><code>RenderFragment&lt;TItem&gt;?</code></td><td>Custom item content.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>TimeZone</code></td><td><code>TimeZoneInfo</code></td><td>Decides days and hours. Defaults to <code>TimeZoneInfo.Local</code>.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Clock</code></td><td><code>TimeProvider</code></td><td>The source of today and now; replace it in tests. Defaults to <code>TimeProvider.System</code>.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>

		<h5>State</h5>
		<table class="table table-sm">
			<thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>Date</code> / <code>DateChanged</code></td><td><code>DateOnly?</code></td><td>The focused date, which decides the period shown; null means today.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>View</code> / <code>ViewChanged</code></td><td><code>CalendarView</code></td><td><code>Month</code> (default), <code>Week</code> or <code>Agenda</code>.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>AvailableViews</code></td><td><code>IReadOnlyList&lt;CalendarView&gt;</code></td><td>The views offered by the switcher.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>SelectedItem</code> / <code>SelectedItemChanged</code></td><td><code>TItem?</code></td><td>The selected item.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>FirstDayOfWeek</code></td><td><code>DayOfWeek</code></td><td>Defaults to Monday.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>MinDate</code>, <code>MaxDate</code></td><td><code>DateOnly?</code></td><td>Days outside are disabled and navigation stops at them.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>IsLoading</code></td><td><code>bool</code></td><td>Shows the busy overlay.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>

		<h5>Layout and appearance</h5>
		<table class="table table-sm">
			<thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>FirstVisibleHour</code>, <code>LastVisibleHour</code></td><td>0, 24</td><td>The local hours shown by the week view.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>SlotHeight</code></td><td>48</td><td>Pixels per hour in the week view.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>MinItemHeight</code></td><td>22</td><td>The smallest height of a week view item; short items are also kept apart in packing.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>ScrollHeight</code></td><td>36rem</td><td>The maximum height of the week view before it scrolls.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>ScrollToHour</code></td><td>null</td><td>Scrolls the week view to an hour when shown, using the library's common module.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>MaxItemsPerDay</code></td><td>3</td><td>Items listed in a month day before a "+n more" button, which opens that day's agenda.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>AgendaDays</code></td><td>7</td><td>Days listed by the agenda, starting at the focused date.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>NowIndicator</code></td><td>true</td><td>A line at the current time in the week view, moved every minute.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>ShadeWeekends</code>, <code>WeekendDays</code></td><td>true, Sat and Sun</td><td>Weekend shading.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>DayCssClassSelector</code></td><td>null</td><td>Extra classes for a day.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>TimeFormat</code></td><td>HH:mm</td><td>The format of times.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>ShowToolbar</code>, <code>ShowNavigation</code>, <code>ShowToday</code>, <code>ShowTitle</code>, <code>ShowViewSwitcher</code></td><td>true</td><td>Hide the toolbar or any part of it.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>EmptyText</code>, <code>AriaLabel</code>, <code>CssClass</code></td><td></td><td>Text for an empty agenda, the accessible name and extra root classes.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
	</section>

	<section id="events">
		<h2 class="doc-section">Events</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><code>OnVisibleRangeChanged</code>: <code>(DateTimeOffset From, DateTimeOffset To)</code>, raised on first show and on every change of range.</li>
			<li><code>OnItemSelected</code>: an item was clicked or activated with Enter. <code>SelectedItemChanged</code> is raised only when the selection changes.</li>
			<li><code>OnItemDoubleClick</code>: an item was double clicked.</li>
			<li><code>OnSlotSelected</code>: an empty hour slot (week view) or a day (month and agenda views) was chosen, giving the instant it starts.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			The component also has methods for use through a reference: <code>NavigateAsync(periods)</code>,
			<code>GoToTodayAsync()</code>, <code>GoToDateAsync(date)</code>, <code>SetViewAsync(view)</code>,
			<code>ShowDayAgendaAsync(date)</code> and <code>CanNavigate(periods)</code>, plus the read-only
			<code>CurrentDate</code>, <code>CurrentView</code>, <code>CurrentSelection</code>, <code>VisibleRange</code> and
			<code>Title</code>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section id="keyboard">
		<h2 class="doc-section">Keyboard and accessibility</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>The month and week views are ARIA grids; the focused day or hour is the grid's active descendant.</li>
			<li><kbd>Left</kbd> and <kbd>Right</kbd> move a day; <kbd>Up</kbd> and <kbd>Down</kbd> move a week in the month view, an hour in the week view and a day in the agenda.</li>
			<li><kbd>Enter</kbd> or <kbd>Space</kbd> selects the focused day or hour; <kbd>Page Up</kbd> and <kbd>Page Down</kbd> change period; <kbd>Home</kbd> goes to today.</li>
			<li>Items are buttons, reachable with <kbd>Tab</kbd>, with an accessible name giving title, date and times.</li>
			<li>Transitions are turned off for users who prefer reduced motion.</li>
			<li>Below 576 pixels wide the month view shows each item as a dot; the agenda view is recommended there.</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section id="time-zones">
		<h2 class="doc-section">Time zones and daylight saving</h2>
		<p>
			Items are instants (<code>DateTimeOffset</code>), and <code>TimeZone</code> decides which day and hour they fall
			in. The week view's hour axis is made of real elapsed hours: on the day the clocks go forward that day's column
			has no slot for the skipped hour, and in the week the clocks go back the repeated hour gets a row of its own,
			labelled with both UTC offsets. Each day header notes a day of 23 or 25 hours, and items are drawn exactly as
			long as they really last. Open the clock change week on the demo tab to see it.
		</p>
		<p>
			The arithmetic is in public static helpers, usable on their own: <code>CalendarMath</code> (visible dates and
			ranges, navigation, the start and length of a day, wall clock to instant), <code>CalendarLayoutEngine</code>
			(splitting items by day and packing overlaps into columns) and <code>CalendarTimeAxis</code> (the week view's
			hour axis).
		</p>
	</section>

	<section id="styling">
		<h2 class="doc-section">Styling</h2>
		<p>
			The calendar uses Bootstrap's buttons and colours, follows <code>data-bs-theme</code> and the operating system's
			dark mode, and exposes CSS variables such as <code>--pd-calendar-item-bg</code>, <code>--pd-calendar-item-fg</code>,
			<code>--pd-calendar-weekend</code>, <code>--pd-calendar-accent</code> and <code>--pd-calendar-now</code>. Set
			the item variables in a class returned from <code>CssClassSelector</code> to colour items by category.
		</p>
	</section>

</div>
